/-
  GPn6T.lean — generalized Petersen graphs GP(n,6), n ≥ 13: the colouring (tables and definitions).

  GP(n,6) = `GPk.gp n 6` (see GPPeriodic.lean): u_i = 2i, v_i = 2i+1; edges 3i: u_i u_{i+1}, 3i+1: u_i v_i,
  3i+2: v_i v_{i+6}.  Colouring: for n ≥ 27 a periodic part of period 7 (patterns P0..P6; block
  J < n - n mod 7 - 7 gets P_(J mod 7)) followed by a seam of length n mod 7 + 7 that depends on n mod 7;
  explicit colourings for 13 ≤ n < 27.  A pattern is [outer, spoke, inner] with colours 0..4.
  The tables were found by a SAT search on 2026-10-02 (search/gpsearch.py, search/gp6.json); this file was generated
  by search/gen_gpk.py.  The Lean proof does not depend on the search: all windows are checked by `decide`.
-/
